1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:06,660
Last summer, we visited a bank in Kunming, but this bank holds life instead of money.
去年夏天，我们参观了昆明的一家银行，不过这家银行存放的不是钱，而是生命。

2
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:11,350
It’s called the Germplasm Bank of Wild Species in Southwest China.
它叫作中国西南野生生物种质资源库。

3
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:20,190
Its seed bank, the largest one in Asia, keeps nearly 100,000 collections from over 11,000 kinds of wild plants.
它的种子库是亚洲最大的，保存着近10万份种子样本，来自1.1万多种野生植物。

4
00:00:20,990 --> 00:00:24,450
We learned that many scientists made hard journeys to fill this bank.
我们了解到，许多科学家为了充实这座种子库，走过了艰苦的旅程。

5
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:30,490
They climbed mountains, crossed highlands, and traveled through forests to collect valuable seeds.
他们攀登高山、穿越高原、穿过森林，去采集珍贵的种子。

6
00:00:31,290 --> 00:00:41,810
One scientist, Li Heng, led more than 20 trips to high mountains—even after the age of 61—and got badly hurt after falling from the back of a horse during her work.
其中一位科学家李恒带队前往高山20多次，甚至过了61岁仍是如此；她还曾在工作中从马背上摔下来，伤得很重。

7
00:00:42,610 --> 00:00:44,010
But nothing could stop her.
但是，什么也拦不住她。

8
00:00:44,810 --> 00:00:48,970
She often said to her team, “Choose one thing, and give yourself to it.”
她常对团队成员说：“选定一件事，就全身心地投入进去。”

9
00:00:49,770 --> 00:00:57,720
Another scientist, Guo Yongjie, collected seeds from Mount Qomolangma at 6,212 meters above sea level.
另一位科学家郭永杰在珠穆朗玛峰海拔6212米处采集了种子。

10
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:01,600
This is the highest place ever for collecting plant seeds.
这是迄今为止采集植物种子的最高地点。

11
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:07,860
He spent over 200 days a year in the wild, just to add one more kind of plant seed to the bank.
他每年在野外度过200多天，只为给种子库再增添一种植物的种子。

12
00:01:08,660 --> 00:01:10,650
“A seed is hope,” one scientist shared.
“一颗种子就是希望。”一位科学家分享道。

13
00:01:11,450 --> 00:01:19,650
These seeds are not just tiny plant parts; they carry genes that may help us grow better crops, make new medicines, or bring back lost forests.
这些种子不只是植物的微小部分；它们携带着基因，这些基因可能帮助我们种出更好的庄稼、研制新药，或是恢复已经消失的森林。

14
00:01:20,450 --> 00:01:24,200
But some kinds of plants are disappearing, and we may lose them forever.
但一些植物种类正在消失，我们可能会永远失去它们。

15
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,570
Therefore, collecting valuable seeds is a race against time.
因此，采集珍贵的种子是在与时间赛跑。

16
00:01:29,370 --> 00:01:32,180
It is a job that needs patience, courage and love.
这是一项需要耐心、勇气和爱心的工作。

17
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:34,870
Saving seeds is everyone’s job.
保护种子是每个人的责任。

18
00:01:35,670 --> 00:01:38,120
Such seed banks are not only found in China.
这样的种子库并非只在中国才有。

19
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:48,550
By working with seed banks in Norway, the UK, and some other countries around the world, the scientists can turn these treasures into a shared hope for the far future.
通过与挪威、英国以及世界上其他一些国家的种子库合作，科学家们能把这些宝藏变成对遥远未来的共同希望。

20
00:01:49,350 --> 00:01:55,480
As we left, we had a deeper respect for the scientists who have spent their lives on this quiet but great work.
离开的时候，我们对这些科学家的敬意更深了，他们把一生都投入到了这项默默无闻却伟大的工作中。

21
00:01:56,280 --> 00:02:01,450
The seeds they save carry life, hope, and a better future for all living things on the earth.
他们保护的种子承载着生命、希望，以及地球上所有生物更美好的未来。
